W# Cached parallel spin-+2 projections

Load `Plus2ProjectionCachedParallel.wl` **after** the existing Teff source-construction section and after the spheroidal-table cache section.

The cleaned implementation changes the parallelization strategy. It no longer creates one task per `ell`. Instead, it evaluates the compiled Teukolsky source once on each angular grid at a given radial point and applies every `ell` projection in a single matrix multiplication. The cached spheroidal tables are loaded on the master kernel once per `m`.

## Required existing definitions

```wl
centralRule
omegaOfM[m]
sphValsOnRule[s, m, omega, ellList, rule]
plus2TfunOfM[m]
patchLeftProd["XGrid"]
patchRightProd["XGrid"]
```

The default spheroidal provider is `sphValsOnRule`. This should be the cache-aware accessor from the table-generation section. When the actual disk-cache accessor has another name, pass it through the option:

```wl
"SphValuesProvider" -> yourCachedSphValuesAccessor
```

## Load

```wl
Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], "Plus2ProjectionCachedParallel.wl"}]];
```

or use the full path returned by Finder.

## Preflight

Your generated tables use the `s = -2` basis, so the default `"BasisSpin" -> -2` matches them.

```wl
preflightPlus2CachedProjector[
  2,
  5,
  centralRule
]
```

Inspect:

```wl
%["MaxIdentityError"]
```

It should be close to machine precision, consistent with your earlier orthogonality check.

## Single-m test

```wl
patchAssocProd = <|
  "Left"  -> patchLeftProd["XGrid"],
  "Right" -> patchRightProd["XGrid"]
|>;

plus2TestM2 = runPlus2ProjectionForM[
  2,
  patchAssocProd,
  plus2TfunOfM[2],
  centralRule,
  "EllMax" -> 5
];
```

The projected arrays are stored compactly as matrices:

```wl
Dimensions /@ plus2TestM2["ProjectionMatrices"]
```

Rows correspond to radial points and columns correspond to the `ellList` recorded in metadata:

```wl
plus2TestM2["Metadata", "ellList"]
```

A backward-compatible per-`ell` view is also retained under:

```wl
plus2TestM2["Data"]
```

## Production run

```wl
plus2Manifest = runPlus2ProjectionsAllMCached[
  15,
  patchAssocProd,
  plus2TfunOfM,
  centralRule,
  "MList" -> Range[-15, 15],
  "Overwrite" -> False,
  "ReturnResults" -> False
];
```

Each completed `m` mode is atomically saved. Rerunning with `"Overwrite" -> False` resumes by skipping existing mode files. The cache path includes hashes of the angular rule, the left/right radial grids, and the projection convention, so a later `nX = 256` run cannot accidentally reuse an `nX = 128` result.

## Normalization check

The projector includes `"PhiFactor" -> 2 Pi` by default because your cached one-dimensional angular norms were approximately `1/(2 Pi)`. This is the full-sphere normalization inferred from the orthogonality check. Before a long production run, compare one small projected mode against the old implementation to confirm that its Fourier convention does not already absorb this factor.

## Grid convention

The harmonic tables are evaluated on:

```wl
centralRule["yGrid"]
```

while the Teff source function is evaluated on the paired mixed-coordinate values:

```wl
-r0val centralRule["yGrid"]
```

The code keeps those paired grids together and never independently sorts the mixed-coordinate values.
